<title>HUNGARY: Hungary two-yr govt bond yield rises to 18.48 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary two-yr govt bond yield rises to 18.48 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Hungary's two-year government bonds was set at 18.48 percent at an auction on Thursday, up from 18.42 percent set at an auction one month ago, th Government Debt Management Agency (AKK) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>    First day of interest period    23 June 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity		    24 July 1999</p>
<p>    Total on offer			10,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received		 19,471.15 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated		     10,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued			  13,000 million forintd</p>
<p>    Average annual yield		18.48 pct</p>
<p>    Average price			 97.94 pct</p>
<p>    Maximum price			 98.17 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: The bond bears a fixed interest rate of 16.5 percent, payable semi-annually starting from January 24, 1998.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
